# Accessibility — component guidance

- Prefer semantic HTML (`button`, `nav`, `main`, `aside`) before ARIA. Use shadcn primitives from `@/components/ui/*` — Radix handles roles, focus trap, and keyboard behavior for dialogs, selects, and tooltips.
- Every interactive control needs an accessible name: visible text, `aria-label`, or `aria-labelledby`. Icon-only buttons require `aria-label`; pair decorative icons with `aria-hidden="true"` when a label is present elsewhere.
- Form fields: associate `<label htmlFor={id}>` with controls, or use `aria-label` on standalone inputs (e.g. search bars). Toggle/filter chips expose state with `aria-pressed`.
- Images: meaningful `alt` from context (`asset.prompt`); decorative images use `alt=""`.
- Dialogs: every `DialogContent` includes `DialogTitle`; add `DialogDescription` when extra context helps screen-reader users.
- Keyboard: nested interactive elements inside clickable containers must not steal or bubble activation. Call `stopPropagation()` on **both** `onClick` and `onKeyDown` for inner controls. Never nest `<button>` inside `<button>` — restructure the card surface instead.
- Focus: preserve visible focus styles (`focus-visible:ring-*`). Do not remove outlines without a replacement.
- Motion: respect `prefers-reduced-motion` when adding animations via `motion`.
- Tests: assert with `getByRole` and `getByLabel`; add `data-testid` only when roles are not unique.
